blocks, where $r_i,s_j\\in\\{1,2\\}$ are the block sizes. Let $q=r_is_j\\le4$ and compute $\\delta(M_{ij})$ from [[lem-small-block-determinant-separation-lower-bound]]. If $\\det(M_{ij})=0$, return `singular-pivot`; if $\\det(M_{ij})\\ne0$ and $\\delta(M_{ij})\\le\\tau$, return `pivot-separation-failure` because the requested pivot bound is not certified. Otherwise use the cofactor adjugate formula of [[lem-adjugate-inverse-formula-over-a-field]] to set $\\operatorname{vec}(Y_{ij})=\\operatorname{adj}(M_{ij})\\operatorname{vec}(F_{ij})/\\det(M_{ij})$ and store $Y_{ij}$. The local dimension is at most four in the real block case and one in the complex triangular case.\n\n4. After all blocks are solved, return `success` and $X=UYV^*$, together with the exact residual $C-(AX+XB)$. No computed Schur candidate is accepted as an exact factorization unless step 2 verifies its defining equalities.",
